# Code quality (Syraa)

All new or changed code must pass repo checks before merge.

## Commands (repo root)

```bash
npm run check      # lint + format check + typecheck (TS) + ruff (Python)
npm run format     # auto-fix TS (Biome) + Python (Ruff)
npm run test       # vitest (packages/*, apps/*) + pytest (ingest-worker)
```

## TypeScript (`packages/*`, `apps/*`)

- **Biome** — lint + format (`biome.json` at root)
- **tsc --noEmit** — each workspace package exposes `typecheck` script
- **Vitest** — unit/integration tests in package `tests/`
- **`@syraa/harness`** — chat orchestration (LLM, lessons → memory); no Mastra import in domain packages
- Functional factories preferred over classes (except small Error types)
- **Postgres + Redis** in Docker Compose for app services

## Python (`services/ingest-worker/`)

- **Ruff** — lint + format (root `pyproject.toml`, src under `services/ingest-worker/`)
- **pytest** — tests under `services/ingest-worker/tests/`
- PDF ingest and heading heuristics only — do not add Python app SDKs

## Adding a new package

1. Create under `packages/<name>/` or `apps/<name>/` (auto-included in npm workspaces)
2. Add `typecheck`, `test`, and `build` scripts to `package.json`
3. TypeScript is covered by root Biome config — no per-package ESLint needed
4. Run `npm run check && npm run test` from repo root

## Adding a new Python service

1. Create under `services/<name>/` with its own `Dockerfile` if containerized
2. Register paths in root `pyproject.toml` (`tool.ruff.src`, `tool.pytest`)
3. Set `PYTHONPATH` in `scripts/dev/python.sh` if the service exposes importable modules
